IV=2DD=3A MAKE_RAID_LUNS UTILITY

   There is a new utility that is available starting with OSF=2F1 V3=2E2=2D=
A=2E
   It is in the =2Fdev directory and is called MAKE_RAID_LUNS=2E  It uses t=
he
   naming format of =22rzxnn=22=28rza17=29=2E It can be used for creating a=
ll special
   files for any single LUN on an HSZ40=2E  That is; it will create all fil=
es=2C
   block and character for all partitions for an HSZ40 unit=2E

   This saves from invoking the mknod utility 16 times of each HSZ40 unit=
=2E

   To invoke this utility use the following procedures=3A

    =23cd =2Fdev  =2D changes working directory to =2Fdev
    =23MAKE_RAID_LUNS rza17  =2D this will create all special files for the=
 HSZ40
                             unit D100 on Host Side SCSI Bus 2=2E

    When using this utility=2C the =22nn=22 portion of the file names must =
be
    correct=2E  It should be calculated by the same formula that was discus=
sed
    previously=2E


    nn =3D =28 8 * Host Side SCSI Bus =23 =29 =2B =28 Target ID from HSZ40 =
unit number=29

    Another Example=3A

    To create special files for HSZ40 unit D202 on SCSI Bus 2=3A

    =23cd =2Fdev
    =23MAKE_RAID_LUNS rzc18

    This utility will have to be run for each separate HSZ40 unit=2E Be sur=
e
