IV=3A     MAKEDEV UTILITY

    This utility is located in the =2Fdev directory=2E  This section is bas=
ed
    upon OSF=2F1 version 3=2E2=2D4 and below=2E

    MAKEDEV is a script that can be used to create device special files=2E
    However=2C it requires that a specific naming format be used=2E  For SC=
SI
    devices it requires the following format=3A

    rzxxx

    The =22xxx=22 can only be numeric characters=2E  Here are some examples=
=3A

    rz0=2C rz10=2C rz130=2C etc=2E

    Also the =22xxx=22 number will determine the SCSI Host Side Bus number =
and
    the SCSI Target=2E  The LUN is assumed to be 0 in all cases=2E  The
    calculations are as follows=3A

    SCSI Host Side Bus Number =3D  Integer of =28 xxx =2F 8 =29

    The remainder of the above division=2C if any=2C will be the Target ID=
=2E

    MAKEDEV will calculate the minor number=2C based upon the same calculat=
ion
    that was used in the previous examples=2C except that the LUN is always=
 0=3A

   =28 16384 * SCSI Host Bus =23 =29 =2B =28 Target ID * 1024=29 =2B =28LUN=
 * 64=29 =2B Partition

   EXAMPLE=3A  Using a unit name of RZ16  =3D 16 is the =22 xxx=22

   SCSI Host Side Bus Number =3D =28 16 =2F 8 =29 =3D 2  with a remainder o=
f 0=2E

   Minor number for rz16a =3D

  =28 16384 * 2 =29 =2B =28 0 * 1024 =29 =2B =28 0 * 64 =29 =2B 0 =3D 32768

   MAKEDEV will then invoke mknod=2C using the major number associated with=
 that
   device type and the calculated minor number=2E  It will create all speci=
al
   files for all partitions=2C both block mode and character mode=2E

   If you were going to associate the device name RZ16 to an HSZ40 unit=2C =
which
   unit would that be=3F

   Remember than an HSZ40 unit has the designator DTZL=3A

   T =3D Target ID
   Z =3D 0
   L =3D Lun

   Remember that RZ16 was on SCSI Host Side Bus =23 2=2C Target ID of =220=
=22=2C
   LUN of =220=22=2E

   The RZ16 device would relate to HSZ40 unit D000 or D0 that was connected
   to the Host Adapter on SCSI Host Side Bus =23 2 =2E

   So if you use MAKEDEV to create special files=2C you give the device an
   OSF=2F1 device name that will produce the correct minor number=2E  Also=
=2C you
   CANNOT use MAKEDEV to create special files for any HSZ40 units whose uni=
t
   designator do not end in =220=22=2E  As an example=2C you can=27t use MA=
KEDEV for
   D101=2E  This would be TARGET ID =221=22=2C but LUN =221=22=2E  MAKEDEV =
always assumes
   LUN to be =220=22=2E

   EXAMPLE OF INVOKING MAKEDEV=3A  =2Fdev=2FMAKEDEV rz16

=0C                                                                       P=
age 18

IV=2DA=3A  ANOTHER EXAMPLE=3A

   You want to use the device name rz161 and use MAKEDEV to create the spec=
ial
   files=2E  What HSZ40 unit would this name point to if you use MAKEDEV to
   create the special files=3F

   SCSI Host Side Bus Number =3D =28 161 =2F 8 =29 =3D 20 with a remainder =
of 1=2E
   The Target ID is then equal to this remainder=2C which is 1=2E

   LUN is always 0=2C so using the =22DTZL=22 HSZ40 unit format=2E  This wo=
uld be
   D100 on the HSZ40 that is on the Host Adapter on Host Side SCSI bus 20=
=2E

   The point of all these examples is to show that you cannot just pick any
   arbitrary OSF=2F1 device name if you are going to use MAKEDEV to create
   the special files=2E  You must be sure that the minor number that MAKEDE=
V
   is going to calculate will identify the correct HSZ40 Unit on the correc=
t
   Host Side SCSI Bus=2E

