V=3A HELPFUL UTILITIES

      The OSF=2F1 =22file=22 utility can be used to determine if an HSZ40 u=
nit
      can be accessed from the OSF=2F1 Host System=2E  Here is the procedur=
e=3A

      For this example=2C an HSZ40 has a unit D101=2E From the HSZ40 CLI=2C=
 issue
      the following command=3A      hsz40>set =22xx=22 noread
      Be sure to enable the unit=27s read cache when the testing is complet=
ed=2C by
      using the following command=3A hsz40>set =22xx=22 read

      The =22xx=22 represents the HSZ40 unit designator that will be tested=
=2E
      Example=3A      hsz40>Set D101 noread

      This command disables the read cache for the unit=2E  The reason is t=
o
      allow a visual indication that the unit is indeed being accessed=2E  =
This
      will cause the information to be accessed from the unit rather than f=
rom
      the cache=2C if the information is in cache=2E

      From the OSF=2F1 Host System issue the following command=3A

      =2Fusr=2Fbin=2Ffile =2Fdev=2Fxxxx

      The =22xxxx=22 represents the OSF=2F1 character mode partition device=
 special
      file that represents the HSZ40 unit=2E

      EXAMPLE=3A      =2Fusr=2Fbin=2Ffile =2Fdev=2Frrzb17a

      In this case the special file for rrzb17a has already been created=2E

      The device activity indicator =28green light=29 should light up on
      the device=2E If the unit is a multi=2Ddevice container only one of t=
he
      devices that is part of that container will light=2E

      Also on the OSF=2F1 system=2C the following output should be seen aft=
er the
      command is issued=3A

 =2Fdev=2Frrzb17a character special =288=2Fmmmm=29 SCSI =23 n HSZ40 disk =
=23xxx =28SCSI ID =23t=29

     The =228=22 is the major number
     The =22mmmm=22 should be the minor number
     The =22n=22 should be the SCSI Host Side Bus number
     The =22t=22 should be the target ID as used in the HSZ40 unit DTZL=2C =
where
       the =22T=22 in the DTZL HSZ40 unit matches the =22t=22 from the file=
 command=2E
     The =22xxx=22 is the Disk Number=2C which was discussed in a previous =
section=2E

     If an error is seen such as=3A

     file=3A  Cannot get file status on =2Fdev=2Fmmmm
     =2Fdev=2Fmmmm=3A  cannot open for reading

     This error usually indicates that the special file in the
     =2Fdev directory that matches =22mmmm=22 doesn=27t exist=2E

     If the only output that is returned from the file command is the major
     and minor number=2C then either the device is not answering or
     the device special file does not have the correct minor number=2E  Che=
ck
     the minor number to be sure that it matches the correct SCSI Host Side
     Bus number and the correct HSZ40 TARGET ID and LUN from the HSZ40 unit
     designator=2E

