VIII=3A CONFIGURATION FILE ENTRIES USING THIS OSF=2F1 NAMING SCHEME

     In current versions of OSF=2F1=2C including V3=2E2=2D4=2C the OSF=2F1 =
boot startup
     procedures will not recognize the name format =22rzxnn=22=28rza17=29=
=2E  Also the
     iostat utility will not recognize the =22rzxnn=22 format=2E  The next =
sections
     will discuss procedures for use of the =22rzxnn=22 format for the conf=
iguration
     file and for using iostat=2E

     These procedures require editing the configuration file and then rebui=
lding
     the kernel from the new configuration file=2E

     =21=21 BE SURE TO SAVE THE OLD CONFIGURATION FILE AND KERNEL
     BEFORE EDITING AND REBUILDING=2E

     The format for an entry in the configuration is as follows=3A

    disk device rznn    at scsiz    drive  mmm

    The =22nn=22 is calculated as=3A

      nn =3D =28 8 * Host Side SCSI Bus =23 =29 =2B =28 Target ID from HSZ4=
0 unit number=29

    The =22z=22 denotes the Host Side SCSI BUS number

    The =22mmm=22 denotes a drive number=2C it is calculated as follows=3A

=2864 * Host SCSI Bus =23=29 =2B =288 * Target ID from HSZ40 Unit=29 =2B LU=
N of HSZ40 unit
=0C
