 Dickinson College

From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Nov 05 14:33:22 1997
From: Unix Administrator <unixadmin () gmd ! com ! pe>
Date: Wed, 05 Nov 1997 14:33:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMM: TLZ09-VA hangs. Can S3Trio64 cause this also?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078619210280

This is a not-implemented-yet summary. After some research, we've found
that there are some known-problems with the TLZ09 drive. These problems
can result on a tape drive hang while running the DU vdump command, or a
tape drive that stops responding when using its compression driver (this
can also happen on NT), and some more problems that I can't recall.
You should check the HW and FW revisions. The last revisions that exist
so far are: HW Rev. A03, FW Rev. 0172.
In our case, the revisions are: HW A01 and FW 0165. We've requested an
upgrade kit (suppose it's a software kit) that should correct these
problems. We are not sure about something: is enough to apply the
firmware upgrade, even when the HW revision is an old one ?
	Our thanks to:

Dave Cherkus
Robert L. McMillin


