Dear Gurus,

> I got a strange problem with my NIS. If box A is setup as NIS slave
> server, it isn't able to get master servers auto.master map. If box A
> is setup as client everything is working.
> Can't get master of auto.master. Reason: no such map in server's domain.
> Can't get master of auto.home. Reason: no such map in server's domain.
> Can't get master of auto.direct. Reason: no such map in server's domain.

Thanks to 

Spider Boardman <spider@Orb.Nashua.NH.US>
Paul A Sand <pas@unh.edu>
Rainer Freis <freis@santix.de>

Following Spider's advice, I copied the maps with

	./ypxfr -f -h `ypwhich -m group.byname` auto.master
	./ypxfr -f -h `ypwhich -m group.byname` auto.home
	./ypxfr -f -h `ypwhich -m group.byname` auto.direct

After this, the slave server knows about the auto.* maps and copies
these maps with usual ypxfer options. 

Gerhard

