From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 04 10:26:43 1997
From: William Whitehead <William_Whitehead () byu ! edu>
Date: Tue, 04 Nov 1997 10:26:43 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Starting DU 4.0a if fstab is bad
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078619210228

Well, I guess it was 1 am in the morning, and it would have helped to use
my brain.  I figured out how to do what I needed.  I got some thoughts
going when I read another message on the list.  Here is how I fixed my problem

1. I halted the DEC Station with the halt button on the back.
2. I then set the AUTO_ACTION variable to HALT.  Just in case I needed to
restart it again.
3. I then used the Generic unix kernel and booted into single user mode by
doing:
	boot -fl s -fi genvmunix
4. This took me into single-user mode where I was able to mount the file
systems with:
	mount -a
5. I was then able to fix my /etc/fstab file
6. I reset the AUTO_ACTION variable to RESTART.  
7. Restarted the machine and it came up again.

Sorry to waste everyone's bandwidth on a brain cramp.  Thanks anyway!

Bill


