Thanks to the following people who responded within 15 minutes.

Jim Belonis <belonis@dirac.phys.washington.edu>
lombardi emanuele <lele@mantegna.casaccia.enea.it>
Robert Schuhl <robert.schuhl@ald-vt.de>
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com (Alan Rollow - Dr. File System's Home for Wayward  
 Inodes.)

The solution was quite easy, actually.

Halt (crash) the system, boot single user mode (boot -flag s), run bcheckrc to 
automount the filesystems, use vi to edit the /etc/passwd file, add user root 
without a password, reboot the system either via shutdown or Ctrl-D. (I used the 
latter)

Again, thanks for the people of this list who always come through!

Regards,

Johan Erlank


