Subject: SUMMARY: DU 4.0 and Memory Use
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078619210454

Thanks everyone for the rapid and extensive responces.

My original question was:

> Does Digital UNIX 4.0 utilize unallocated system memory to file
caching?

The answer was a resounding YES it does.  This is called UBC (Unified
Buffer Cache) and is a tunable parameter.

One person (Randy Hayman haymanr@icefog.alaska.edu) even pointed me to a
utility 


Put down the mouse, and step away from the keyboard. . . 

